= What the exploratory experiments show <evidence>

*Finding:* the local comparisons did not demonstrate an improvement over baseline. That is a limit on the evidence, not a reason to relabel a successful mechanism check as workflow value or tune answer keys until an intervention wins. The practices remain provisional.

== Earlier work: null results and a withdrawn detour

An initial evidence-challenge smoke test completed three reviews before another job timed out: two deficient packets were blocked, while one clean packet was held for an unrequested reviewer identifier. No matched treatment comparison completed, so this observation did not establish that the challenge caused over-checking. The timeout showed caller termination, not its underlying cause.

Two subsequent development batches produced 46 packet judgments in five fresh agent jobs. All arms agreed on accept-versus-block outcomes; changing the applicability reminder showed no acceptance advantage. Differences between explicit rejection and insufficient evidence were retained rather than relabeled into a gain.

A later checksum exercise showed that standard byte checks detect edits to covered files. It also left unlisted dependencies, identical bytes under the wrong root and post-check recapture unresolved; the comparison was against a revision-label-only shortcut, not the full existing workflow. The optional recipe was withdrawn because successful byte checking had not demonstrated useful agent-level impact and had displaced the core assurance question.

== Core-principle review comparison

The next experiment compared a short requirements-based baseline with each practice separately: two-way review, source-first judgment and consequence-directed optional checks. Six review fixtures covered an omitted language requirement, unjustified telemetry, a justified helper, clean read-only work, insufficient PDF-readability evidence and sufficient link-existence evidence. Four additional fixtures offered one optional check for tenant isolation, deletion scope, refund rounding or a typo.

The fixture observations were supplied facts, not live privacy, deletion or financial workloads. Expected decisions and relevant check choices were fixed before judging and independently checked. A missing required observation was scored as insufficient evidence, not as proof that the artifact itself was defective.

